  "blocks": {
    "\"Our DX is fine — new hires are productive in a week.\"": "“我们的 DX 不错——新人一周内就能开始产出。”",
    "\"Productive because someone sits with them for that week. The agent doesn't get that week; check the AX separately.\"": "“那是因为有人陪他们过了这一周。智能体没有这一周的适应期，要单独检查 AX。”",
    "Agents face the same codebase with none of that accumulation. Stateless across sessions, an agent re-learns the codebase from scratch every time — it benefits from the fast test suite and the clear error messages, but anything it figured out yesterday is gone unless it was written into the environment, which the agent only perceives through tool results. That's the gap AX names: the parts of DX that survive when the developer is an agent, plus concerns humans don't have, like keeping the context window free.": "智能体面对同一个代码库时，却没有人类积累的那部分记忆。智能体跨会话无状态，每次都要从头重新学习代码库——它能从快速测试套件和清晰错误消息中受益，但昨天理解的任何内容都会消失，除非被写入<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/environment\">环境</a>；而智能体只能通过工具结果感知环境。这就是 AX 所命名的缺口：当开发者变成智能体后，DX 中仍然有效的部分，再加上人类不需要面对的关注点，例如为上下文窗口保留空间。",
    "Developer experience — how easy a codebase and its toolchain make it for humans to do good work. Good DX is fast feedback, clear error messages, documentation that answers the question you actually have, and setup that works on the first try. The term long predates AI coding; it's in this dictionary mainly as the contrast for AX.": "DX 即开发者体验（Developer Experience），描述代码库及其工具链让人做好工作的难易程度。良好的 DX 包括快速反馈、清晰错误消息、能够回答实际问题的文档，以及一次设置即可正常工作的开发环境。这个术语早在 AI 编码出现前就已存在；它被收入本词典，主要是为了与 AX 形成对照。",
    "DX is the interaction between the human and the codebase — nothing more. The main difference between the two audiences is that humans are stateful and agents are stateless. A human learns the codebase once and carries that knowledge into every day after, which is why poor DX is survivable: they route around slow CI by batching their pushes, around missing docs by asking in Slack once, around confusing structure by remembering where things live. The workarounds accumulate, and a team ends up productive in a codebase that fights them.": "DX 就是人与代码库之间的交互，仅此而已。两类使用者的主要区别在于：人是有状态的，而智能体是无状态的。人学习一次代码库后，可以把这份知识带到之后每一天，因此糟糕的 DX 仍然可以被克服：他们通过批量推送绕开缓慢 CI，通过在 Slack 问一次来绕开缺失文档，通过记住文件位置来绕开混乱结构。这些变通办法不断累积，团队最终仍能在一个处处与他们作对的代码库中保持生产力。",
    "The overlap means DX investment often improves AX for free — strict types, fast tests, and predictable structure help both. The divergence means it doesn't always: a beautiful onboarding doc helps a human for a week and an agent not at all unless it's reachable from AGENTS.md.": "两者的重叠意味着，投入 DX 往往也会顺带改善 AX——严格类型、快速测试和可预测结构对双方都有帮助。但两者的分歧也意味着这种改善并非总会发生：一份精美的入门文档可以帮助人类一周，却完全帮助不了智能体，除非它能从 AGENTS.md 被发现和读取。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
